      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-200",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Email local part becomes the public leaderboard username for OAuth signups (partial email disclosure to anon).\n\nhandle_new_user falls back to split_part(new.email,'@',1) as profiles.username when signup metadata has no username (always the case for Google OAuth, which the web app offers and never prompts for a username). The anon-readable leaderboard view (004:64-72, granted to anon at 004:72) is owned by the migration role, bypasses profiles RLS, and exposes p.username for every user with a completed run.\n\nImpact: Confidentiality: bulk harvest of email local parts (effectively full addresses for gmail.com users) of OAuth users, linkable to user_id and game history, for phishing and spam. The user can rename later, but the default is exposed from the first completed run.\n\nExploit scenario: A Google-signed-in player finishes a run. Their profile row was created with username = email local part (for gmail.com accounts this is the whole address minus the known domain). Any unauthenticated caller queries the leaderboard view via PostgREST (select=username,user_id,avatar_url) and harvests these values in bulk. username_available('<guess>') also confirms whether an email local part is registered. The migration 005 comment and docs/security/backend-audit.md say profiles are private and the view exposes no emails.\n\nPreconditions: User signed up through Google OAuth (or any path without raw_user_meta_data.username) and did not rename; User has at least one completed run so a leaderboard row exists; Anon key is public, so no credential is needed to query the view.\n\nRecommendation: Do not derive the public username from the email. Generate a neutral handle such as 'jugador_' plus random suffix, or require the user to choose a username before the profile is public. Keep the leaderboard view's username column limited to values the user chose. Backfill existing profiles whose username equals their email local part.\n\nCWE-359. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "supabase/migrations/009_anonymous_guests.sql",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 18,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    coalesce(new.raw_user_meta_data->>'username', split_part(new.email, '@', 1))"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "handle_new_user",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "handle_new_user"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
