        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-307",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Daily ticket cap on seed shopping is bypassed by minting tickets on throwaway guest accounts and claiming them.\n\nstart-run issues tickets to any anonymous Supabase user, and the web client creates those with signInAnonymously at will. claim-run-ticket then moves a guest's ticket to the caller's real account, and the only gate is a count of the target's tickets created in the last day. The claim keeps the ticket's original created_at, so tickets minted more than 24h earlier are not counted and can be claimed without limit.\n\nImpact: Players can pick favourable seeds without bound. That defeats the stated purpose of migration 008, which is to cap seed shopping with a per-user daily limit. The effect is limited to leaderboard fairness. A bot with the public engine can already play any given seed optimally, so no confidentiality or account-level harm follows.\n\nExploit scenario: 1. The attacker signs in anonymously many times, one guest per session. 2. Each guest calls start-run up to 30 times a day and records the server-chosen seeds, which are 0..999999. 3. The attacker precomputes the best seed offline with the public engine and waits 24h, or just claims the best seeds. 4. The attacker signs into a real account and calls claim-run-ticket (10 per minute) with each guest's token. Tickets older than one day add nothing to the target's count, so the claim never hits the daily cap. 5. submit-run accepts a run for the chosen seed because the ticket belongs to the real user.\n\nPreconditions: Supabase anonymous sign-ins enabled (the web client relies on them); Attacker can create multiple guest sessions, limited only by Auth rate limits and the optional IP limiter; Attacker holds a real non-anonymous account to claim into.\n\nRecommendation: Count tickets the target has claimed or been issued over a fixed window, for example by adding a claimed_at column. Alternatively, apply the cap to the ticket's original created_at only if it was issued to that same user. Also limit anonymous ticket issuance per IP and in total, and expire unclaimed or unused tickets after a short TTL.\n\nCWE-799. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
